- I'm Wes Chatham

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:03.030
and here are five shows to check out

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.950
if you loved The Expanse, on Binge Guide.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.440
- Thanks Wes I couldn't
have said it better myself

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.540
and we are big fans of The
Expanse on Amazon Prime.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.390
With three Certified Fresh seasons

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:15.980
filled with galactic
action, existential drama,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.180
and world exploring adventure,
it's not hard to see why.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.150
So if you're a fan
looking for more to love

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.450
after The Expanse,

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.430
we think that these space-veering shows

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.140
will launch your next few binge sessions

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.660
into a new dimension,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.960
starting with our family
friendly pick, "Lost in Space."

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.920
This Netflix reboot of the
TV series of the same name

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.810
follows adventures of the Robinson family

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:39.230
as they navigate the cosmos
after getting lost in space.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:40.400
I mean the title says it all.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.360
What can I say?

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.620
Look beyond the title though,

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.100
and you'll find a modern
take on the classic series

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.230
with something for everyone
in your own family,

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.180
with tons of safe for kids action.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.760
That's coupled with a large heart

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.360
and ambitious production values

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.520
that should attract sci-fi adventure fans.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.760
And with a third and
final season on the way

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.100
you can quickly get caught
up with the first two seasons

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.750
in just about 20 hours
which sounds blissful

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.300
compared to being, you
know, lost in space.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.940
Okay, I'm done sorry.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.610
Next up is our throwback pick

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:10.430
and that is going to
"Battlestar Galactica."

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:12.620
This re-imagining of the '70s TV show

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.150
follows humanity's war
with the android race

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:18.610
known as the Cylons and bucks
the trend of the original spin

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:20.880
on "Star Wars" in favor of a darker tone

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.740
in seriously heady twists
that strongly resonated

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.150
with modern audiences.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.870
With two certified first seasons

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:28.870
and a massive cult following,

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.930
the four season series has been praised

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:34.490
for its addictive high-minded
themes and complex storylines.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:35.730
And it's frequently been called

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.340
one of the greatest
sci-fi series of all time.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.010
With 76 episodes total
you can binge a series

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.610
in about 56 hours,

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:44.540
which is nothing compared
to the amount of time

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.960
you'll spend contemplating
all the storylines.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.950
Another entry into a classic universe

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.870
is our certified fresh
pick "Star Trek Discovery."

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.920
This CBS all access series
six plays roughly a decade

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.880
before "Star Trek" the original series

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.210
and explores the earlier days

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:01.010
of the United Federation
of Planets and the advent

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.680
of war with the Klingons.*

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:06.030
Critics praise "Discovery's"
ability to forge its own path

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.840
while effectively dramatizing
new takes on the Lord

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.280
that results in a solid
franchise installment

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.260
for the next generation of Trek fans.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.850
With three seasons, you can
watch "Star Trek Discovery"

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.610
in about 26 hours after
which you'll have boldly

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.090
gone where no couch has gone before.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.780
Next up is our audience pick

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:26.490
going to the alternative history
series "For All Mankind."

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.160
This Apple TV plus drama
from "Battlestar Galactica"

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.870
creator Ronald D. Moore,
blends true life characters

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.130
with fictional events
like the Russian's landing

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.010
on the moon first.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.060
To ask the question
what would have happened

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.840
if the space race never ended.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.620
With stellar production values,

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.580
incredible cast and some
very timely storylines,

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.500
the show has the right
stuff to be unpredictable

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:47.830
and all inspiring.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.560
You can watch the entire
first season in about 10 hours

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:54.230
and good news, season two is
a go for launch in early 2021

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.830
so be sure to keep a lookout.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.137
And rounding out our
list is our editor's pick

00:02:58.137 --> 00:02:59.740
"Raised By Wolves."

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.010
This Ridley Scott produced HBO Max series

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.130
revisits many of the sci-fi
masters hallmark themes

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:08.710
including androids, space
colonization and lots of action.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.440
All while asking pretty big questions

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.010
about human nature and
what it means to be alive.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:16.000
Critics say the show is filled
with Ridley Scott trademarks

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.590
like imagination and other worldly imagery

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.340
that will stimulate the mind and eye,

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.070
but also adds a surprising
amount of heart.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.330
And with just 10 episodes you can binge

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.580
all of "Raised By Wolves"
in about 10 hours,

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.500
which I hear is how long
it feels to hibernate

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.470
for deep space exploration.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.780
All right friends hopefully
this list will open your eyes

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:36.550
to a whole new galaxy
of content to explore.

